// PNG - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

// PNG: eight signature bytes, then length-prefixed typed chunks,
// each ending in a CRC over its type and data.
//
// There is a chunk for exactly this. tEXt is keyword NUL text --
// the keyword is 1-79 printable Latin-1 characters -- and it exists
// so a file can carry a caption. That is where the greeting goes,
// not in a comment above the file: the format has a field and this
// is what it is for.
//
// The IDAT here is a real zlib stream, because zlib is in the
// standard library and a PNG whose image data is not deflate is
// not a PNG. The CRCs are computed, not transcribed -- every one of
// them is verified by scripts/verify_encodings.py.
//
// png: 104 bytes, dumped sixteen at a time.
//
// The bytes below are not hand-written. They are built from the
// format's own field widths by scripts/build_object_formats.py, and
// scripts/verify_encodings.py reads the fields back by name -- the
// magic number, the lengths, the offsets. A hex dump written from
// memory is wrong in one byte and looks exactly like a correct one.
//

// 89 50 4E 47 0D 0A 1A 0A 00 00 00 0D 49 48 44 52 |.PNG........IHDR|   <- 0000
// 00 00 00 01 00 00 00 01 08 02 00 00 00 90 77 53 |..............wS|   <- 0010
// DE 00 00 00 18 74 45 58 74 44 65 73 63 72 69 70 |.....tEXtDescrip|   <- 0020
// 74 69 6F 6E 00 48 65 6C 6C 6F 20 57 6F 72 6C 64 |tion.Hello World|   <- 0030
// 21 5D CC 10 C2 00 00 00 0B 49 44 41 54 78 9C 63 |!].......IDATx.c|   <- 0040
// 60 00 02 00 00 05 00 01 7A 5E AB 3F 00 00 00 00 |`.......z^.?....|   <- 0050
// 49 45 4E 44 AE 42 60 82                         |IEND.B`.|   <- 0060
